DESCRIPTION >
    Wave 3 aggregated attribution. One row per (source, medium, campaign) with
    conversions=count() and revenue=SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value))),
    serving firstTouchNonDirectAttribution (api/lib/attribution-engine.js:172-229, queryName
    'first_touch_non_direct_attribution'). Faithful 1:1 port.
    FIRST-TOUCH via argMinIf-window, NOT ASOF. The last-touch twin (last_touch_non_direct_by_site.pipe)
    uses per-field ASOF joins, but ASOF always picks the LAST preceding row — it structurally
    CANNOT produce a FIRST (earliest) touch, so an argMax->argMin swap of the ASOF structure is
    impossible (the Wave-3 "money-rail STOP"). Resolved with argMinIf(field, timestamp,
    pv.timestamp <= conv.timestamp): argMinIf picks the field value at the MIN timestamp among
    rows satisfying the condition = the earliest qualifying pageview. Validated this session via
    `tb --cloud deploy --check` (+ bogus-column schema check) — the argMinIf-window pattern the
    flexible_report windowJoin already uses on the live path.
    PER-FIELD null-skip reproduced by argMinIf's inherent val-null-skip: argMinIf(pv.utm_medium, ...)
    ignores rows where utm_medium is NULL, so medium/campaign can come from a DIFFERENT (later)
    touchpoint than source when the earliest non-direct-utm_source pageview has a null in that
    field — exactly matching the live per-field argMin(pv.utm_medium, pv.timestamp) null-skip
    (attribution-engine.js:186-188). No explicit IS NOT NULL needed per field (argMinIf skips nulls).
    NON-DIRECT gate (live :200-202) applied to the whole pageview set: utm_source IS NOT NULL
    AND != '' AND != 'direct'. Window has NO lower bound (live join is only pv.timestamp <=
    e_inner.timestamp, no attributionWindow) — argMinIf condition is pv.timestamp <= conv.timestamp.
    Outer: source = COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_source,''),'direct'), medium = COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_medium,''),
    'none'), campaign = argMinIf over nullIf(utm_campaign,'') (live :177-179 emits campaign||null).
    nullIf makes argMinIf's null-skip ENGAGE on Tinybird's empty-string campaign ('' here vs NULL in
    PostHog) so it credits the earliest REAL campaign like LIVE, not the empty touch. Equality JOIN on distinct_id (live :204,
    NOT the mixed-inequality ON which Tinybird rejects — the timestamp bound moves into argMinIf).
    Typed-column translation (§2.6): properties.site_id -> site_id, event -> event_type; pv fields
    from `events` self-join (pre-filtered subqueries, the flexible_report windowJoin pattern).
    MONEY: revenue toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value)) == live toFloatOrZero(toString(
    e.properties.conversion_value)); conv is 1 row per $conversion (event_id unique) -> value once.
    VALUE-PARITY NOT RUN — founder/orchestrator must value-gate vs live HogQL before wiring/enabling.

NODE first_touch_non_direct_by_site_node
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_source, ''), 'direct') AS source,
        COALESCE(NULLIF(utm_medium, ''), 'none') AS medium,
        utm_campaign AS campaign,
        countIf(lower(coalesce(conversion_type, '')) != 'refund') AS conversions,
        SUM(toFloat64OrZero(toString(conversion_value))) AS revenue
    FROM
    (
        SELECT
            conv.event_id AS event_id,
            conv.conversion_value AS conversion_value,
            -- Thread conversion_type to the outer countIf refund filter. any() (not GROUP BY) so the
            -- argMinIf grouping (event_id unique per conv row) is untouched; any() is deterministic here.
            any(conv.conversion_type) AS conversion_type,
            argMinIf(pv.utm_source, pv.timestamp, pv.timestamp <= conv.timestamp) AS utm_source,
            argMinIf(pv.utm_medium, pv.timestamp, pv.timestamp <= conv.timestamp) AS utm_medium,
            -- nullIf(campaign,'') so argMinIf's val-null-skip ENGAGES on Tinybird's empty-string
            -- campaign representation (Tinybird stores empty utm_campaign as '', not NULL). LIVE reads
            -- PostHog where empty campaign is NULL, so its argMin skips the empty touch and credits a
            -- later REAL campaign; without nullIf, argMinIf here would include '' and diverge. Matches
            -- live argMin(pv.utm_campaign) null-skip (attribution-engine.js:190). source/medium need
            -- no nullIf: medium empties already read as NULL in Tinybird; both COALESCE to a floor.
            argMinIf(nullIf(pv.utm_campaign, ''), pv.timestamp, pv.timestamp <= conv.timestamp) AS utm_campaign
        FROM
        (
            SELECT event_id, distinct_id, timestamp, conversion_value, conversion_type
            FROM events
            WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
              AND event_type = '$conversion'
              AND timestamp >= {{ DateTime(date_from, required=True) }}
              AND timestamp < {{ DateTime(date_to, required=True) }}
        ) AS conv
        LEFT JOIN
        (
            SELECT distinct_id, timestamp, utm_source, utm_medium, utm_campaign
            FROM events
            WHERE site_id = {{ String(site_id, required=True) }}
              AND event_type = '$pageview'
              AND utm_source IS NOT NULL AND utm_source != '' AND utm_source != 'direct'
        ) AS pv ON pv.distinct_id = conv.distinct_id
        GROUP BY conv.event_id, conv.conversion_value
    )
    GROUP BY source, medium, campaign
    ORDER BY revenue DESC
    LIMIT 50000

TYPE endpoint
